Link the system libraries rustc names in the order rustc names them.

meson/query-rustc.py dedups rustc's --print=native-static-libs list through a
Python set, so the order meson links librsvg-2.so against libgcc_s, libm, libc
and the rest follows the interpreter's string hash seed, which is random per
process. The DT_NEEDED order in librsvg-2.so, and with it the library's bytes,
then differ between two builds of the same tree: build_runtime.sh --verify
found libm before libc in one build and after ld-linux in the next.
dict.fromkeys drops the duplicates and keeps the order.

Not yet sent upstream; GNOME/librsvg main still has the set. Drop this patch
when a release orders the list.

--- a/meson/query-rustc.py
+++ b/meson/query-rustc.py
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@
             libs = [removeprefix_fallback(lib, "-l") for lib in libs] # msys2
             print(
                 " ".join(
-                    set(
+                    dict.fromkeys(
                         libs
                     )
                 )
